{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לכן ישכב עמך הלילה", :translit "lachen yishkav imach halailah", :gloss "therefore he shall lie with you tonight"} {:he "על כן לא נקברה עמו במערה", :translit "al ken lo nikberah imo bame'arah", :gloss "therefore she was not buried with him in the cave"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: לכן ('therefore') in the verse foreshadows Leah's exclusion from burial with Jacob"}], :frame {:text "Jacob was buried in the Cave of Machpelah (Genesis 50:13). Leah's burial there is recorded in Genesis 49:31, where Jacob states he buried Leah there.", :sources ["Genesis 49:31" "Genesis 50:13"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לכן", :translit "lachen", :gloss "therefore"} {:he "מדה במדה", :translit "midah bemidah", :gloss "measure for measure"} {:he "כי ילדתי לו", :translit "ki yeladeti lo", :gloss "for I have borne him"} {:he "ג'", :translit "gimel", :gloss "3"} {:he "ו'", :translit "vav", :gloss "6"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "לכן", :b "מדה במדה"}], :frame {:text "Regarding Levi, Leah says כי ילדתי לו at Genesis 29:34, having borne Jacob three sons (Reuben, Simeon, Levi). Regarding Zebulun she says the same phrase at Genesis 30:20, by which point she has borne six sons (Genesis 29:32–30:20). Leah initially expected three sons as her share, since Jacob would have twelve sons split among four wives; bearing six meant a double portion. The principle of מדה במדה (measure for measure) is articulated in the Mishnah (Sotah 1:7) and expanded in the Talmud (Sotah 8b–9b) and Midrash (Bereshit Rabbah).", :sources ["Genesis 29:34" "Genesis 30:20" "Sotah 1:7" "Sotah 8b" "Sotah 9a" "Sotah 9b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: לכן ('therefore') in the verse foreshadows Leah's exclusion from burial with Jacob", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "לכן", :a-value 100, :b "מדה במדה", :b-value 100, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :discipli